# A style guide whose tags claim more than the tooling does

## Rules

- A tag without a rule id says nothing that can be checked. `[tidy]`
- A tidy rule that does not exist. `[tidy:no-such-rule]`
- A clippy lint that the workspace lint table does not switch on. `[clippy:no_such_lint]`
- A rustc lint that the workspace lint table does not switch on. `[rustc:no_such_lint]`
- A dylint lint that nobody declared. `[dylint:nami_no_such_lint]`
- A planned mechanism that is not in the registry. `[planned:no-such-plan]`
- Hooks only give feedback. `[hook]`
- The reference suite does not exist yet. `[reference]`
- A misspelt tag. `[reveiw]`
